        "body": "Workday is a public company, traded as WDAY, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, California. Its SEC filings list a CIK of 0001327811, and its most recent reported revenue, on a 10-K for the period ending 2026-01-31, is 9552000000 US dollars.\n\nOn its own site the company describes itself as an enterprise AI platform for HR, finance, and IT, and promotes Sana and agentic AI, saying its agents can find, build, act, and automate rather than only assist. The product tracked for the company is Workday AI, described as HR and finance AI covering skills-based talent and predictive analytics, with sensitive HR data exposure noted.\n\nThe company appears in litigation records as Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Williams v. Workday, Elias v. Workday, Noriega v. Workday, Hill v. Workday, and Doe v. Workday, filed in district courts in California, Georgia, Colorado, Maryland, and Virginia. Litigation in California accounts for 281 cases.",
